WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.100
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.370 --> 01:34.900
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.229 --> 01:37.810
[Episode 53]

4
01:38.360 --> 01:41.800
Any troops willing to fight against Japanese aggression,

5
01:41.800 --> 01:45.360
regardless of any past or present

6
01:45.560 --> 01:47.310
grudges between them and the Red Army,

7
01:46.990 --> 01:50.840
[Zhang Xueliang, Acting Commander-in-Chief of the Northwestern Bandit-Suppression Headquarters of the KMT Troops]

8
01:47.310 --> 01:49.640
regardless of any differences

9
01:49.830 --> 01:52.880
they may have with the Red Army on domestic issues,

10
01:50.970 --> 01:54.620
[Du Zhongyuan, Chief Distributor of New Life Weekly, patriotic activist]

11
01:52.950 --> 01:55.080
the Red Army will not only immediately

12
01:55.100 --> 01:56.720
cease all hostilities against them,

13
01:56.720 --> 02:00.080
but also stand ready to join hands with them

14
02:00.190 --> 02:01.640
to save our nation.

15
02:03.310 --> 02:04.280
Hanqing,

16
02:04.520 --> 02:07.350
history doesn't give us many chances to choose.

17
02:07.720 --> 02:09.310
You've already missed one.

18
02:09.630 --> 02:11.440
Are you going to make the same mistake again?

19
02:11.440 --> 02:13.160
If we don't step up, who will?

20
02:13.560 --> 02:15.510
If not now, when?

21
02:16.280 --> 02:19.480
Time waits for no one, Hanqing.

22
02:26.160 --> 02:27.470
Zhongyuan,

23
02:29.490 --> 02:31.290
this trip has been well worth it.

24
02:32.750 --> 02:34.550
Zhongyuan, do you have any wine?

25
02:34.720 --> 02:35.240
Of course.

26
02:35.240 --> 02:36.280
Go get some wine, please.

27
02:36.280 --> 02:37.470
I'd like to hear more

28
02:37.470 --> 02:39.310
about your interesting stories involving the Communists.

29
02:39.310 --> 02:39.880
Coming right up.

30
02:39.880 --> 02:41.160
I'll get the wine.

31
02:41.960 --> 02:44.470
After meeting with Du Zhongyuan,

32
02:44.560 --> 02:47.070
Zhang Xueliang became even more determined to reach a truce with the Red Army

33
02:47.070 --> 02:49.670
and join forces against Japanese aggression.

34
02:49.960 --> 02:51.070
While in Shanghai,

35
02:51.310 --> 02:53.440
he also secretly met with his former subordinate,

36
02:53.440 --> 02:55.120
Li Du, a Northeast Volunteer Army commander

37
02:55.120 --> 02:57.550
who had returned from the Soviet Union.

38
02:58.060 --> 02:59.760
He expressed his desire to establish contact

39
02:59.760 --> 03:01.890
with the Communist Party through Li Du

40
03:01.910 --> 03:02.840
and join forces

41
03:03.110 --> 03:06.770
with the Red Army in the northwest to fight the Japanese together.

42
03:09.090 --> 03:12.740
[Wayaobu, Shaanxi]

43
03:11.590 --> 03:13.160
We've been getting reports from all over.

44
03:13.160 --> 03:14.160
The December 9th Student Movement

45
03:14.160 --> 03:15.620
is spreading far and wide.

46
03:15.680 --> 03:16.750
Besides Peiping,

47
03:16.840 --> 03:18.470
students in major cities like Tianjin, Baoding,

48
03:18.470 --> 03:20.240
Taiyuan, Xi'an, Jinan, Hangzhou,

49
03:20.240 --> 03:22.310
and Shanghai have all joined in.

50
03:22.310 --> 03:23.840
It's spreading like wildfire!

51
03:23.840 --> 03:25.970
Just as Comrade Zedong said,

52
03:26.530 --> 03:28.790
the patriotic students are the kindling,

53
03:28.790 --> 03:31.250
and our Communist Party has set them ablaze.

54
03:31.510 --> 03:33.560
This is wonderful news

55
03:33.560 --> 03:34.840
for our national resistance movement.

56
03:34.840 --> 03:35.510
Indeed.

57
03:35.840 --> 03:37.280
And there's more good news.

58
03:37.280 --> 03:38.680
We'll soon be meeting

59
03:38.680 --> 03:40.120
Comrade Zhang Hao (Lin Yuying),

60
03:40.120 --> 03:41.190
the representative sent by the Comintern.

61
03:41.190 --> 03:43.350
It's truly a double celebration today!

62
03:43.350 --> 03:45.150
Make that a triple celebration!

63
03:46.240 --> 03:46.920
There's also Luofu

64
03:46.920 --> 03:49.120
and Comrade Liu Ying's marriage to celebrate.

65
03:49.120 --> 03:51.920
Today, we'll celebrate all 3 occasions together!

66
03:53.590 --> 03:54.400
Runzhi,

67
03:54.840 --> 03:56.000
weren't you supposed to attend a meeting?

68
03:56.000 --> 03:57.680
Why are you suddenly planning to play wedding pranks?

69
03:57.680 --> 03:58.880
I've heard of weddings being held after the fact,

70
03:58.880 --> 04:00.470
but never a belated wedding-night prank.

71
04:00.470 --> 04:02.470
Whether they hold a wedding is up to them.

72
04:02.470 --> 04:04.350
But whether we play a prank on them is up to us.

73
04:04.350 --> 04:06.840
They moved in together without telling anyone.

74
04:06.840 --> 04:07.830
We have to make up for the missed fun!

75
04:07.830 --> 04:09.690
Fine, fine. You're always right.

76
04:10.040 --> 04:10.600
Let's go!

77
04:34.630 --> 04:36.150
He splashed water all over my foot.

78
04:36.150 --> 04:37.150
He saw you?

79
04:38.830 --> 04:39.830
No, he didn't.

80
04:40.600 --> 04:42.330
He wasn't wearing his glasses.

81
04:43.150 --> 04:44.880
He wasn't wearing his glasses?

82
04:45.560 --> 04:46.780
Get him! Get him!

83
04:47.900 --> 04:48.580
Let's go.

84
04:49.150 --> 04:49.830
Luofu.

85
04:50.000 --> 04:51.000
Comrade Luofu.

86
04:51.120 --> 04:52.070
Comrade Luofu.

87
04:52.310 --> 04:53.480
Comrade Luofu.

88
04:54.310 --> 04:55.320
Are you up yet?

89
04:56.040 --> 04:57.770
Could you come out for a moment?

90
04:57.950 --> 04:58.830
Luofu.

91
04:58.950 --> 05:00.360
I'm up. I'm up.

92
05:02.120 --> 05:03.800
Why is everyone here so early?

93
05:04.070 --> 05:06.470
Wasn't the meeting supposed to start at 10?

94
05:16.110 --> 05:19.040
Weren't you just splashing water outside?

95
05:20.560 --> 05:21.710
How did you know?

96
05:21.710 --> 05:23.640
You splashed it right onto my foot.

97
05:23.890 --> 05:25.710
I thought I caught a glimpse of someone.

98
05:25.710 --> 05:26.640
So it was you.

99
05:27.150 --> 05:27.950
Sorry about that.

100
05:27.950 --> 05:29.000
I wasn't wearing my glasses.

101
05:29.000 --> 05:30.830
Why weren't you wearing your glasses?

102
05:30.830 --> 05:32.030
I just got up, didn't I?

103
05:32.030 --> 05:33.480
Why are you only getting up now?

104
05:33.480 --> 05:34.920
Weren't we supposed to have a meeting?

105
05:34.580 --> 05:36.370
[He Zizhen, Mao Zedong's Wife]

106
05:35.210 --> 05:36.570
Are you not feeling very well?

107
05:36.570 --> 05:38.120
No, no. I'm perfectly fine.

108
05:38.270 --> 05:39.750
You look a little pale.

109
05:39.970 --> 05:40.790
You're looking rather nervous, too.

110
05:40.790 --> 05:41.950
What have you been up to?

111
05:41.950 --> 05:43.390
He's a little nervous, actually.

112
05:43.390 --> 05:44.310
Am I nervous?

113
05:44.310 --> 05:45.390
Aren't you?

114
05:45.830 --> 05:46.370
I...

115
05:47.750 --> 05:49.350
Have I done something wrong?

116
05:50.600 --> 05:51.630
Think about it.

117
05:55.040 --> 05:56.040
Think carefully.

118
05:57.950 --> 05:58.710
How are we supposed to know

119
05:58.710 --> 06:00.000
what you did wrong?

120
06:01.710 --> 06:03.000
I haven't done anything.

121
06:03.000 --> 06:06.270
If you can't figure it out, we're just going to stand here forever.

122
06:06.270 --> 06:07.680
You can stand there all you want. I still haven't done anything.

123
06:07.680 --> 06:08.560
Luofu.

124
06:08.600 --> 06:10.530
You've committed a grave offense!

125
06:13.600 --> 06:15.040
First, you didn't send out wedding invitations.

126
06:15.040 --> 06:16.510
Second, you didn't treat us to a wedding feast.

127
06:16.510 --> 06:19.360
You two just secretly moved your belongings in.

128
06:19.480 --> 06:21.000
And started living together!

129
06:21.000 --> 06:22.150
What kind of behavior is that?

130
06:22.150 --> 06:23.390
This is serious. Do you understand that?

131
06:23.390 --> 06:23.920
Wouldn't you say this is serious?

132
06:23.920 --> 06:24.480
Very serious!

133
06:24.480 --> 06:25.540
Now, about this...

134
06:25.600 --> 06:26.680
Let me explain everything.

135
06:26.680 --> 06:27.880
Who wants to hear your explanation?

136
06:27.880 --> 06:28.800
We want to see the bride!

137
06:28.800 --> 06:29.830
-Exactly! -That's right!

138
06:29.830 --> 06:32.230
We want the bride to come out and explain herself!

139
06:32.230 --> 06:33.070
-Liu Ying! -Liu Ying!

140
06:33.070 --> 06:34.390
-Liu Ying! Come out! -Come on! Liu Ying!

141
06:34.390 --> 06:36.000
I'll explain it myself, then. It's all the same.

142
06:36.000 --> 06:37.240
It's all the same, Comrade Zedong.

143
06:37.240 --> 06:38.510
We don't want to hear your explanation.

144
06:38.510 --> 06:39.070
Don't even try that!

145
06:39.070 --> 06:40.409
Here's what happened...

146
06:40.409 --> 06:41.440
Liu Ying! Liu Ying!

147
06:41.440 --> 06:41.920
Comrade Zedong.

148
06:41.920 --> 06:43.440
Liu Ying, we're coming in!

149
06:43.560 --> 06:44.440
Liu Ying!

150
06:45.240 --> 06:47.070
What a beautiful bride!

151
06:53.600 --> 06:55.460
Why hasn't the bride come out yet?

152
06:55.560 --> 06:56.630
Fine, she won't come out.

153
06:56.630 --> 06:57.830
But why aren't any of you coming out either?

154
06:57.830 --> 06:58.480
Exactly.

155
06:58.540 --> 07:00.620
The bride can't come out on her own!

156
07:00.640 --> 07:02.840
The groom has to come and invite her out!

157
07:04.360 --> 07:05.620
I'll go invite her out.

158
07:06.000 --> 07:06.600
Luofu.

159
07:06.920 --> 07:08.950
How exactly are you going to invite her out?

160
07:08.950 --> 07:09.190
I...

161
07:09.190 --> 07:11.880
We want you to carry the bride out in your arms!

162
07:12.120 --> 07:13.190
Carry her out?

163
07:14.630 --> 07:16.690
Let me make it a little harder for you.

164
07:18.240 --> 07:20.440
I can't believe you'd come up with that!

165
07:33.810 --> 07:34.480
Why are you blushing?

166
07:34.480 --> 07:35.150
Listen!

167
07:35.800 --> 07:36.880
The moment the groom went in,

168
07:36.880 --> 07:38.240
the bride got all shy.

169
07:38.360 --> 07:39.360
That was Zizhen.

170
07:40.190 --> 07:41.650
You'll have to excuse her.

171
07:43.150 --> 07:43.920
Zizhen!

172
07:44.140 --> 07:45.550
Enough laughing.

173
07:45.680 --> 07:47.080
Let's get this over with!

174
07:56.360 --> 07:57.440
Put me down!

175
07:58.270 --> 07:59.320
Put me down!

176
08:02.070 --> 08:03.040
Put me down!

177
08:03.040 --> 08:03.700
Put me down!

178
08:11.560 --> 08:12.480
Give them back.

179
08:20.120 --> 08:21.040
Chairman,

180
08:21.440 --> 08:23.120
it's not that we didn't want to treat everyone,

181
08:23.120 --> 08:23.920
but as you can see,

182
08:23.920 --> 08:25.120
we have neither money

183
08:25.150 --> 08:26.480
nor anything to offer.

184
08:26.880 --> 08:29.010
We can't even afford a bowl of peanuts.

185
08:29.560 --> 08:30.600
How about this?

186
08:30.950 --> 08:32.240
We'll owe you a wedding feast for now.

187
08:32.240 --> 08:33.350
When we have something to spare,

188
08:33.350 --> 08:34.250
we'll make it up to everyone.

189
08:34.250 --> 08:35.780
-Yes. -How does that sound?

190
08:36.360 --> 08:37.909
This young fellow seems sincere.

191
08:37.909 --> 08:39.960
All right. We'll take a rain check.

192
08:40.240 --> 08:40.909
But

193
08:41.000 --> 08:44.000
you'll have to make it up to us when you have a baby, too!

194
08:44.120 --> 08:46.200
We don't want to wait too long, you know!

195
08:46.200 --> 08:47.120
Great!

196
08:52.080 --> 08:52.750
Great!

197
08:54.060 --> 08:55.460
What a lively gathering!

198
08:55.480 --> 08:56.540
Comrade Zhang Hao?

199
08:56.550 --> 08:57.480
Comrade Enlai.

200
08:57.790 --> 08:58.840
Comrade Zhang Hao!

201
08:58.840 --> 09:00.320
Quick, come on in!

202
09:00.580 --> 09:03.000
Comrade Zedong has been waiting for you for ages.

203
09:03.000 --> 09:03.800
Chairman Mao.

204
09:03.950 --> 09:05.440
It's been 10 years since we last met!

205
09:05.440 --> 09:06.800
At the 7th Congress of the Comintern,

206
09:06.800 --> 09:08.060
the delegation spoke highly of our Party,

207
09:08.060 --> 09:09.430
saying it had produced many outstanding leaders

208
09:09.430 --> 09:10.630
and talented statesmen.

209
09:10.630 --> 09:11.510
The very first person they mentioned

210
09:11.510 --> 09:13.030
was you, Comrade Mao Zedong.

211
09:13.030 --> 09:14.090
Comrade Zhang Hao.

212
09:14.510 --> 09:15.670
I've been eager to see you

213
09:15.670 --> 09:17.510
ever since I heard you were coming.

214
09:17.510 --> 09:18.720
It's just that we ran into

215
09:18.410 --> 09:21.880
[Lin Yuying (Zhang Hao), Member of the CPC Delegation to the Comintern]

216
09:18.720 --> 09:20.150
some delays along the way.

217
09:20.150 --> 09:20.790
Perfect timing.

218
09:20.790 --> 09:23.360
Today, let's share in the newlyweds'

219
09:23.390 --> 09:24.670
wedding festivities

220
09:24.720 --> 09:25.870
and hear the valuable insights

221
09:25.870 --> 09:27.830
you've brought back from Moscow.

222
09:28.080 --> 09:28.880
Gladly.

223
09:34.880 --> 09:35.940
Comrade Zhang Hao,

224
09:36.130 --> 09:37.870
we must thank you for bringing us

225
09:37.870 --> 09:40.750
the guiding principles of the 7th Comintern Congress.

226
09:40.750 --> 09:43.430
The Comintern resolution calling for a broad

227
09:43.600 --> 09:45.630
united front against fascism

228
09:45.840 --> 09:48.170
is entirely in line with our own thinking.

229
09:50.030 --> 09:52.720
The August 1 Declaration proposed by our Party's delegation

230
09:52.720 --> 09:54.460
has also laid the groundwork

231
09:54.490 --> 09:56.380
for establishing a national united front

232
09:56.380 --> 09:58.000
against Japanese aggression.

233
09:58.000 --> 09:58.750
I believe

234
09:58.750 --> 10:00.550
we urgently need to convene

235
10:00.670 --> 10:02.080
an enlarged meeting of the Politburo

236
10:02.080 --> 10:05.270
and incorporate the strategy of establishing a national united front

237
10:05.270 --> 10:06.910
against Japanese aggression into a formal resolution.

238
10:06.910 --> 10:07.720
Furthermore,

239
10:07.790 --> 10:10.030
we must quickly

240
10:10.030 --> 10:12.160
settle on our next military strategy.

241
10:13.320 --> 10:14.270
Indeed.

242
10:14.630 --> 10:16.430
Winter is approaching in northern Shaanxi.

243
10:16.430 --> 10:19.090
We're already struggling with hunger and cold,

244
10:19.200 --> 10:21.550
and we're surrounded by hundreds of thousands

245
10:21.550 --> 10:22.910
of KMT troops.

246
10:24.030 --> 10:25.600
Unless we break this deadlock soon,

247
10:25.600 --> 10:27.030
we may not even survive,

248
10:27.270 --> 10:28.930
let alone fight the Japanese.

249
10:29.750 --> 10:30.480
I suggest

250
10:30.480 --> 10:32.280
that before the formal meeting,

251
10:32.600 --> 10:33.630
we circulate this issue

252
10:33.630 --> 10:36.030
among all the corps of the 1st Front Red Army

253
10:36.270 --> 10:37.600
and solicit opinions

254
10:38.240 --> 10:40.030
from all senior commanders.

255
10:44.600 --> 10:45.660
Comrade Zhang Hao,

256
10:46.630 --> 10:48.670
Luofu mentioned in his letter

257
10:48.840 --> 10:50.100
that Comrade Wang Ming

258
10:50.150 --> 10:52.810
agrees with the Zunyi Conference resolutions.

259
10:52.960 --> 10:53.720
That's right.

260
10:53.720 --> 10:55.320
After Comrade Chen Yun arrived in Moscow,

261
10:55.320 --> 10:56.260
he briefed Comrade Wang Ming

262
10:56.260 --> 10:57.840
on what had happened at the Zunyi Conference.

263
10:57.840 --> 10:59.100
I was there at the time.

264
10:59.390 --> 11:00.960
Comrade Wang Ming said that, in principle,

265
11:00.960 --> 11:02.720
he endorsed the resolutions of the Zunyi Conference

266
11:02.720 --> 11:04.200
and decided to have Comrade Chen Yun

267
11:04.200 --> 11:06.330
report on the matter to the Comintern.

268
11:06.480 --> 11:08.750
Comrade Zhang Hao also brought us the radio codes.

269
11:08.750 --> 11:10.020
Unfortunately, our only

270
11:10.020 --> 11:11.080
long-range, high-powered radio

271
11:11.080 --> 11:12.910
was lost while crossing the Xiang River.

272
11:12.910 --> 11:14.390
So we're still unable

273
11:14.390 --> 11:16.600
to establish direct contact with the Comintern.

274
11:16.600 --> 11:17.600
Even so,

275
11:17.750 --> 11:20.270
having the support of Comrade Wang Ming and the Comintern

276
11:20.270 --> 11:21.840
for the Zunyi Conference

277
11:21.960 --> 11:23.360
will certainly help us handle

278
11:23.360 --> 11:25.220
our relations with Zhang Guotao.

279
11:25.320 --> 11:26.380
Comrade Zhang Hao,

280
11:26.670 --> 11:29.240
what's your view on Zhang Guotao's telegram

281
11:29.240 --> 11:30.840
announcing that he has set up

282
11:30.910 --> 11:32.570
his own "Central Committee"?

283
11:34.150 --> 11:35.770
When I first arrived in northern Shaanxi,

284
11:35.770 --> 11:38.170
Comrade Luofu briefed me on the situation.

285
11:38.240 --> 11:39.910
I'm familiar with the dispute

286
11:39.910 --> 11:41.880
over whether to march south or north.

287
11:41.880 --> 11:43.510
But I never imagined

288
11:43.510 --> 11:45.560
things had become this serious.

289
11:46.600 --> 11:48.830
From the very beginning, we have tried every possible means

290
11:48.830 --> 11:51.240
to keep Zhang Guotao united with us

291
11:51.370 --> 11:54.670
and win him over, despite his divisive actions.

292
11:55.670 --> 11:56.750
Throughout this process,

293
11:56.750 --> 11:58.720
we have also done everything in our power

294
11:58.720 --> 12:01.510
to persuade him to change course and bring him back.

295
12:01.510 --> 12:02.510
To be frank,

296
12:02.550 --> 12:03.430
a situation like this,

297
12:03.430 --> 12:04.550
if mishandled,

298
12:04.550 --> 12:05.670
could easily escalate into

299
12:05.670 --> 12:07.270
a life-and-death struggle.

300
12:07.590 --> 12:09.640
Yet you've made every effort

301
12:09.670 --> 12:11.390
to prevent bloodshed.

302
12:11.410 --> 12:12.940
I deeply admire and am moved

303
12:12.960 --> 12:15.820
by the Central Committee's efforts in this matter.

304
12:17.360 --> 12:19.240
Everything we've done

305
12:19.600 --> 12:21.200
has been aimed at preventing

306
12:21.600 --> 12:24.120
a split within the Party and the Red Army.

307
12:24.940 --> 12:27.870
After all, most of our comrades don't know the truth.

308
12:28.400 --> 12:30.330
They've simply been misled by him.

309
12:31.960 --> 12:34.150
I'll send a telegram to Zhang Guotao as soon as possible

310
12:34.150 --> 12:35.690
to inform him that I've arrived in northern Shaanxi

311
12:35.690 --> 12:37.490
and find out what he's thinking.

312
12:43.640 --> 12:48.080
[Renjiaba, Lushan, Sichuan]

313
12:59.480 --> 13:04.790
[Lin Yuying]

314
13:11.840 --> 13:12.880
Chairman Zhang.

315
13:14.360 --> 13:15.240
Xiangqian.

316
13:17.150 --> 13:18.000
Chairman Zhang.

317
13:18.000 --> 13:19.420
I went to the Confidential Communications Bureau on an errand.

318
13:19.420 --> 13:21.630
I heard that Peng Dehuai wiped out an entire division of the Northeast Army

319
13:21.630 --> 13:23.480
and an additional regiment

320
13:23.550 --> 13:24.880
in the battle at Zhiluo Town a few days ago.

321
13:24.880 --> 13:26.340
They even sent us a report.

322
13:27.480 --> 13:28.200
Really?

323
13:29.150 --> 13:30.320
You haven't heard?

324
13:32.200 --> 13:33.480
Perhaps I've just been

325
13:33.790 --> 13:35.430
too busy lately.

326
13:37.750 --> 13:38.680
Chairman Zhang.

327
13:40.480 --> 13:43.540
Why don't we issue a bulletin celebrating the victory?

328
13:44.120 --> 13:46.210
The Central Red Army has won such a major battle.

329
13:46.210 --> 13:47.120
It would be a tremendous boost

330
13:47.120 --> 13:48.350
to our morale.

331
13:49.630 --> 13:50.630
Xiangqian.

332
13:53.200 --> 13:56.360
Watch your wording just now.

333
13:57.360 --> 13:58.360
"The Central"?

334
13:58.670 --> 14:00.130
Which side is the Central?

335
14:23.320 --> 14:24.150
Bocheng.

336
14:25.240 --> 14:25.910
Commander-in-Chief.

337
14:25.910 --> 14:26.630
Come in.

338
14:27.910 --> 14:28.720
Bocheng.

339
14:29.880 --> 14:31.140
Commander-in-Chief.

340
14:32.270 --> 14:33.200
Why is your room

341
14:33.390 --> 14:35.080
like an ice cellar?

342
14:36.640 --> 14:38.100
Why haven't you lit a fire?

343
14:38.320 --> 14:40.150
My firewood is rationed.

344
14:40.200 --> 14:41.270
I'm saving a little for tonight

345
14:41.270 --> 14:42.550
when I go to bed.

346
14:44.880 --> 14:46.270
No need to burn it now. No need.

347
14:46.270 --> 14:47.030
Save it for tonight.

348
14:47.030 --> 14:48.170
That's all the firewood I have.

349
14:48.170 --> 14:49.480
What difference does it make when I burn it?

350
14:49.480 --> 14:50.150
No need. Don't burn it.

351
14:50.150 --> 14:50.630
But...

352
14:50.630 --> 14:51.600
Save it for tonight.

353
14:51.600 --> 14:52.390
Fine, fine.

354
14:54.030 --> 14:54.790
All right.

355
14:56.390 --> 14:57.320
I have some hot water here, too.

356
14:57.320 --> 14:58.270
Good, good.

357
15:02.030 --> 15:03.400
Here, warm your hands.

358
15:22.750 --> 15:23.370
All right.

359
15:24.600 --> 15:25.790
Commander-in-Chief,

360
15:25.790 --> 15:26.670
I heard things

361
15:27.150 --> 15:29.010
haven't been easy for you either.

362
15:32.670 --> 15:34.630
They've withdrawn my personal guards.

363
15:34.630 --> 15:35.630
In the middle of the night,

364
15:35.630 --> 15:38.120
they even took my horse away and slaughtered it.

365
15:38.120 --> 15:40.270
They also accused Kang of being my informant

366
15:40.270 --> 15:42.150
and transferred her to the Women's Movement Committee,

367
15:42.150 --> 15:43.670
ten kilometers away.

368
15:43.880 --> 15:44.960
What a petty move!

369
15:45.510 --> 15:46.540
They're doing this

370
15:46.540 --> 15:47.690
to isolate me.

371
15:48.010 --> 15:49.670
And they're afraid I'll run away.

372
15:49.670 --> 15:51.120
Zhang Guotao doesn't know

373
15:51.120 --> 15:52.030
that I would

374
15:52.550 --> 15:54.390
never abandon my troops.

375
15:55.960 --> 15:57.600
As Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army,

376
15:57.600 --> 15:59.860
I'll eventually lead the Left Route Army

377
15:59.960 --> 16:02.890
in the direction demanded by the Central Committee.

378
16:03.550 --> 16:04.810
Commander-in-Chief,

379
16:04.840 --> 16:06.360
I understand what you're saying,

380
16:06.360 --> 16:08.160
but you still need to be careful.

381
16:09.030 --> 16:10.030
Don't worry.

382
16:10.430 --> 16:12.840
Dong Zhentang has assigned several comrades

383
16:12.840 --> 16:14.080
to ensure my safety.

384
16:14.790 --> 16:15.670
Besides,

385
16:16.030 --> 16:17.430
things are different now.

386
16:17.430 --> 16:18.830
Zhang Guotao's approach

387
16:19.430 --> 16:20.910
is losing support by the day.

388
16:20.910 --> 16:21.960
He's probably

389
16:22.320 --> 16:24.180
too preoccupied to target me now.

390
16:25.910 --> 16:27.170
Commander-in-Chief,

391
16:27.430 --> 16:29.360
you seemed quite excited just now.

392
16:29.630 --> 16:31.240
Is there some good news?

393
16:33.980 --> 16:34.900
There is.

394
16:37.430 --> 16:38.150
Look.

395
16:39.910 --> 16:41.790
Student movements have broken out across the country.

396
16:40.640 --> 16:42.360
[Students from Several Peiping Schools Held a Protest Yesterday]

397
16:41.880 --> 16:43.790
They're demanding an end to the civil war

398
16:43.790 --> 16:45.000
and national unity against Japanese aggression.

399
16:45.000 --> 16:45.880
Excellent!

400
16:46.880 --> 16:49.390
I remember what Chairman Mao said

401
16:49.720 --> 16:51.630
before we crossed the snow-capped mountains.

402
16:51.630 --> 16:52.890
He predicted back then

403
16:53.000 --> 16:55.910
that the Chiang Kai-shek government's appeasement of Japan

404
16:55.910 --> 16:58.170
and its disastrous policy of abandoning North China

405
16:58.170 --> 16:59.480
would inevitably meet with

406
16:59.480 --> 17:02.480
fierce opposition from patriots across the country.

407
17:02.720 --> 17:04.880
The resistance movement would also reach

408
17:04.880 --> 17:05.950
a new peak.

409
17:06.359 --> 17:08.290
That's what made Mao so brilliant.

410
17:08.430 --> 17:09.950
This proves even more clearly

411
17:09.950 --> 17:12.990
that our strategy of marching north to fight the Japanese was correct.

412
17:12.990 --> 17:16.050
The whole nation is talking about resisting Japan now.

413
17:16.520 --> 17:17.710
But what about us?

414
17:17.940 --> 17:20.079
We're still stuck deep in these mountains,

415
17:20.079 --> 17:22.390
locked in a pointless military standoff

416
17:22.470 --> 17:23.839
with the enemy.

417
17:24.150 --> 17:26.430
And even this military standoff

418
17:26.990 --> 17:29.190
probably won't last much longer.

419
17:29.710 --> 17:31.080
The KMT troops' encirclement

420
17:31.080 --> 17:32.600
is steadily tightening.

421
17:35.520 --> 17:36.090
Bocheng.

422
17:37.710 --> 17:40.430
You're an instructor at the Red Army Academy now,

423
17:40.430 --> 17:43.560
yet you're still thinking like a chief of staff.

424
17:46.710 --> 17:49.840
Zhang Guotao won't hold out much longer.

425
17:50.470 --> 17:51.800
We must keep working

426
17:51.880 --> 17:53.340
to win over more comrades.

427
17:53.910 --> 17:54.990
We have to believe

428
17:55.950 --> 17:58.150
this train that's gone off track

429
17:58.150 --> 18:00.480
will eventually get back on the right one.

430
18:03.080 --> 18:04.840
Comrade Liu Zhidan, this way.

431
18:09.190 --> 18:10.720
Are you Comrade Liu Zhidan?

432
18:11.950 --> 18:13.230
This is Chairman Mao.

433
18:18.880 --> 18:19.840
Comrade Zhidan.

434
18:20.120 --> 18:21.050
Good to meet you.

435
18:21.080 --> 18:22.540
Greetings, Chairman Mao.

436
18:23.150 --> 18:25.040
Come on, let me introduce you.

437
18:25.230 --> 18:26.760
This is one of our brave

438
18:26.800 --> 18:28.260
female Red Army soldiers.

439
18:28.430 --> 18:29.670
Her name is He Zizhen.

440
18:30.150 --> 18:32.010
Nice to meet you, Comrade Zhidan.

441
18:32.140 --> 18:33.250
Runzhi has been talking about you nonstop

442
18:32.890 --> 18:37.390
[Liu Zhidan, Deputy Director of the Rear Office of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission]

443
18:33.280 --> 18:34.040
ever since he heard you were coming.

444
18:34.040 --> 18:35.140
He's been waiting outside all afternoon.

445
18:35.140 --> 18:36.800
We've been looking forward to your arrival!

446
18:36.800 --> 18:38.520
Nice to meet you, Comrade Zizhen.

447
18:38.520 --> 18:39.670
She calls me Runzhi

448
18:39.800 --> 18:42.150
because she's my wife.

449
18:42.710 --> 18:45.840
In the local Northern Shaanxi dialect, she's my "poyi."

450
18:46.040 --> 18:46.760
It's warmer indoors.

451
18:46.760 --> 18:47.900
Shall we go inside and talk?

452
18:47.900 --> 18:48.850
It's rather dark in there.

453
18:48.850 --> 18:50.450
The sunlight is lovely here.

454
18:50.480 --> 18:52.340
Why don't we sit out here and talk?

455
18:52.880 --> 18:54.840
We might as well get a feel for the local soil in northern Shaanxi.

456
18:54.840 --> 18:55.190
How does that sound?

457
18:55.190 --> 18:55.760
Sounds good.

458
18:55.760 --> 18:56.630
Come on.

459
18:56.800 --> 18:57.660
Let's sit here.

460
18:58.950 --> 18:59.560
Come on.

461
19:02.520 --> 19:03.120
Do you smoke?

462
19:03.120 --> 19:03.760
Yes.

463
19:06.040 --> 19:06.760
Here.

464
19:07.990 --> 19:08.920
I'll smoke this.

465
19:09.810 --> 19:10.880
All right, all right.

466
19:10.880 --> 19:12.280
Go ahead and smoke yours.

467
19:25.520 --> 19:26.770
Comrade Zhidan, here.

468
19:26.770 --> 19:28.040
Have some hot water.

469
19:28.800 --> 19:29.840
Okay. Thank you.

470
19:36.080 --> 19:37.120
Comrade Zhidan,

471
19:38.150 --> 19:42.360
you and so many comrades in Shaanxi and Gansu have been through a lot.

472
19:44.800 --> 19:45.990
Chairman Mao.

473
19:46.910 --> 19:48.710
The Central Committee saved us.

474
19:48.880 --> 19:51.210
We're grateful to the Central Committee.

475
19:52.670 --> 19:55.040
It was you who established and preserved

476
19:55.060 --> 19:56.840
this revolutionary base in northern Shaanxi,

477
19:56.840 --> 19:59.230
giving the Central Committee somewhere to take refuge.

478
19:59.230 --> 20:00.430
In that sense,

479
20:00.560 --> 20:02.360
we mustn't let left opportunism

480
20:02.560 --> 20:05.620
destroy this revolutionary base in northern Shaanxi.

481
20:05.630 --> 20:07.910
Now that the Central Committee is here,

482
20:08.470 --> 20:10.600
things will be much easier from now on.

483
20:11.230 --> 20:11.790
Good.

484
20:12.600 --> 20:13.630
Comrade Zhidan,

485
20:14.080 --> 20:15.400
Enlai told me about

486
20:15.420 --> 20:17.020
your conversation with him.

487
20:17.630 --> 20:18.600
I fully agree

488
20:18.810 --> 20:19.670
with your views on the various aspects

489
20:19.670 --> 20:22.800
of the work in the Northern Shaanxi revolutionary base.

490
20:22.840 --> 20:23.630
I've also

491
20:23.630 --> 20:25.630
discussed this with Comrade Luofu.

492
20:26.280 --> 20:27.850
We must arrange new assignments as soon as possible

493
20:27.850 --> 20:32.120
for the comrades who were wrongly purged during the anti-counterrevolutionary campaign.

494
20:32.120 --> 20:33.180
That's wonderful!

495
20:33.430 --> 20:34.960
As for your own assignment,

496
20:35.550 --> 20:38.890
the Central Committee has also given it careful consideration.

497
20:38.890 --> 20:41.620
This is a good opportunity to discuss it with you.

498
20:42.910 --> 20:44.170
There are 2 positions.

499
20:45.080 --> 20:45.740
The first is

500
20:45.850 --> 20:47.630
Deputy Director of the Rear Services Office

501
20:47.630 --> 20:49.840
of the newly established Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission.

502
20:49.840 --> 20:51.970
Comrade Enlai will serve as Director.

503
20:52.990 --> 20:53.800
The second is

504
20:54.080 --> 20:58.010
Garrison Commander of Wayaobu, where the Central Committee is based.

505
20:58.150 --> 20:59.080
Comrade Zhidan,

506
20:59.520 --> 21:00.470
what do you think

507
21:00.710 --> 21:01.950
of these 2 positions?

508
21:03.760 --> 21:05.160
Thank you, Chairman Mao.

509
21:06.910 --> 21:07.880
I think...

510
21:08.560 --> 21:09.710
I won't...

511
21:09.710 --> 21:11.560
I won't choose.

512
21:11.880 --> 21:14.150
As long as I can continue serving the Party,

513
21:14.150 --> 21:15.880
I'll take whatever assignment

514
21:15.880 --> 21:16.800
the Central Committee gives me.

515
21:16.800 --> 21:17.470
Good.

516
21:17.670 --> 21:20.230
Then you'll take on

517
21:20.470 --> 21:22.330
both positions I just mentioned.

518
21:24.320 --> 21:25.230
Chairman Mao, this...

519
21:25.230 --> 21:26.860
This isn't just my decision.

520
21:27.470 --> 21:29.910
It was discussed and approved by the Politburo.

521
21:29.910 --> 21:30.880
Comrade Zhidan,

522
21:31.430 --> 21:32.960
do you have any objections?

523
21:36.830 --> 21:38.280
None at all.

524
21:41.160 --> 21:43.420
I'm grateful for the Party's trust in me.

525
21:43.560 --> 21:46.130
I will carry out the tasks entrusted to me by the Party without fail.

526
21:46.130 --> 21:48.610
Good. I'm glad you agree.

527
21:48.880 --> 21:49.940
In a couple of days,

528
21:50.120 --> 21:51.990
we're planning to

529
21:52.150 --> 21:54.120
gather the comrades from northern Shaanxi

530
21:54.120 --> 21:55.360
for a discussion.

531
21:55.600 --> 21:56.730
When the time comes,

532
21:56.910 --> 21:58.840
I'd like you to help us get everyone on board.

533
21:58.840 --> 22:00.900
Let's all sit down together and talk.

534
22:00.910 --> 22:02.120
Speak from the heart.

535
22:02.430 --> 22:04.960
Share your grievances and let off some steam.

536
22:04.990 --> 22:07.670
Let's put the past behind us.

537
22:07.740 --> 22:09.170
We must stay united

538
22:09.520 --> 22:10.780
and look to the future.

539
22:12.840 --> 22:13.800
All right.

540
22:14.600 --> 22:15.630
Wonderful.

541
22:16.360 --> 22:17.420
That's wonderful!

542
22:19.190 --> 22:20.150
Runzhi,

543
22:20.860 --> 22:21.810
it's only been a little while,

544
22:21.810 --> 22:23.760
and the northwest wind has already blown the water cold.

545
22:23.760 --> 22:25.430
Why don't you all go inside and continue talking?

546
22:25.430 --> 22:27.670
Isn't this northwest wind part of life here?

547
22:27.670 --> 22:28.930
It's a good chance to experience the local customs.

548
22:28.930 --> 22:30.190
We'll stay right here.

549
22:30.390 --> 22:32.390
I feel I've known Zhidan all my life.

550
22:32.910 --> 22:35.630
Comrade Zhidan is an honest, decent man.

551
22:35.840 --> 22:37.320
It's a shame we didn't meet sooner.

552
22:37.320 --> 22:38.720
Thank you, Chairman Mao.

553
22:43.840 --> 22:44.800
Zhidan,

554
22:46.310 --> 22:47.710
tell me more about the situation in northern Shaanxi

555
22:47.710 --> 22:49.190
in greater detail.

556
22:50.520 --> 22:51.520
All right.

557
22:55.470 --> 22:58.040
Liu Zhidan gave Mao Zedong a detailed report

558
22:58.190 --> 23:00.520
on the development of the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base,

559
23:00.520 --> 23:02.080
the state of the revolutionary struggle,

560
23:02.080 --> 23:03.080
the building of the armed forces,

561
23:03.080 --> 23:06.230
and the progress of work among the people.

562
23:06.630 --> 23:08.120
He also gave an honest account

563
23:08.120 --> 23:10.720
of his own ideas on how to carry out these tasks.

564
23:10.840 --> 23:11.810
His sincerity and modesty

565
23:11.810 --> 23:14.230
left a deep impression on Mao Zedong.

566
23:14.520 --> 23:16.430
Mao felt an immediate connection with him.

567
23:16.430 --> 23:19.000
As Mao Zedong later recalled,

568
23:19.470 --> 23:20.430
"When I arrived in northern Shaanxi,

569
23:20.430 --> 23:22.560
I had met Liu Zhidan only once,

570
23:22.700 --> 23:23.200
yet I could tell

571
23:23.200 --> 23:25.660
he was an excellent Communist Party member.

572
23:25.840 --> 23:26.880
Not long afterward,

573
23:26.880 --> 23:28.800
the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission

574
23:28.800 --> 23:31.040
appointed Liu Zhidan to 2 more positions:

575
23:31.040 --> 23:32.600
Commander-in-Chief of the Northern Route Army

576
23:32.600 --> 23:34.600
and Commander of the 28th Red Army.

577
23:42.190 --> 23:43.120
Guirong.

578
23:43.840 --> 23:44.670
Guirong.

579
23:44.990 --> 23:45.720
You're back!

580
23:47.800 --> 23:49.190
Did you meet Chairman Mao?

581
23:49.190 --> 23:50.150
I did.

582
23:50.710 --> 23:51.800
What did he say?

583
23:53.840 --> 23:55.170
The skies have cleared.

584
23:55.320 --> 23:56.650
The skies have cleared?

585
23:56.710 --> 23:58.910
Chairman Mao and I had a wonderful talk.

586
23:58.920 --> 24:00.120
He asked me all sorts of questions

587
24:00.120 --> 24:02.650
about the situation here in northern Shaanxi

588
24:02.910 --> 24:04.320
and sought my opinions.

589
24:04.670 --> 24:05.630
What's more,

590
24:05.880 --> 24:07.470
the Central Committee has decided

591
24:07.470 --> 24:09.120
to reinstate me.

592
24:10.230 --> 24:11.230
And

593
24:11.430 --> 24:13.270
Vice Chairman Zhou is about to convene

594
24:13.270 --> 24:14.570
a meeting with comrades from northern Shaanxi

595
24:14.570 --> 24:17.050
to hear everyone's views.

596
24:17.210 --> 24:19.870
Don't you think the skies have finally cleared!

597
24:21.040 --> 24:22.240
They certainly have!

598
24:22.710 --> 24:24.080
That's wonderful!

599
24:24.560 --> 24:25.520
You must be hungry.

600
24:25.520 --> 24:28.040
Come, sit down. I'll get you something to eat.

601
24:28.040 --> 24:28.990
I'm hungry.

602
24:29.090 --> 24:29.950
Now that I'm so happy,

603
24:29.950 --> 24:31.040
I'm even hungrier.

604
24:31.150 --> 24:32.470
The food's still warm.

605
24:33.080 --> 24:33.950
Here.

606
24:35.950 --> 24:38.480
Eat while you tell me

607
24:38.640 --> 24:40.570
what else Chairman Mao said to you.

608
24:44.190 --> 24:45.040
You...

609
24:45.880 --> 24:47.760
Make a pair of padded cotton shoes.

610
24:47.760 --> 24:50.420
Chairman Mao asked you to make him cotton shoes?

611
24:50.560 --> 24:51.310
No.

612
24:52.320 --> 24:54.150
I saw Chairman Mao

613
24:54.360 --> 24:56.820
wearing a pair of patched cloth shoes today.

614
24:57.200 --> 24:58.190
In this freezing weather,

615
24:58.190 --> 25:00.230
how can a southerner like him stand the cold?

616
25:00.230 --> 25:01.910
Make him a pair of padded cotton shoes.

617
25:01.910 --> 25:03.310
The thicker, the better.

618
25:03.880 --> 25:04.530
All right.

619
25:09.560 --> 25:10.320
Zhidan,

620
25:10.950 --> 25:12.330
do you know

621
25:12.360 --> 25:13.820
Chairman Mao's shoe size?

622
25:17.280 --> 25:18.880
We talked so much about work.

623
25:19.230 --> 25:20.390
I never got around to asking.

624
25:20.390 --> 25:21.580
If you don't know his size,

625
25:21.580 --> 25:23.050
how am I supposed to make them?

626
25:23.050 --> 25:24.800
If they're too small, they'll pinch his feet.

627
25:24.800 --> 25:27.080
If they're too big, they won't fit properly.

628
25:27.080 --> 25:29.430
Chairman Mao is tall,

629
25:29.760 --> 25:31.120
and he has broad feet, too.

630
25:31.120 --> 25:32.310
His feet are about

631
25:32.700 --> 25:34.020
this much longer

632
25:34.280 --> 25:35.630
and this much wider than mine.

633
25:35.630 --> 25:36.910
You say this much longer

634
25:36.910 --> 25:37.760
and this much wider.

635
25:37.760 --> 25:39.080
But how much exactly?

636
25:39.280 --> 25:41.340
How am I supposed to get the fit right?

637
25:43.360 --> 25:44.430
Come with me.

638
25:45.800 --> 25:46.950
We were sitting

639
25:47.080 --> 25:48.610
right in front of the steps.

640
25:48.670 --> 25:50.040
The Chairman had his feet

641
25:50.040 --> 25:52.040
resting on the stone slabs like this.

642
25:52.040 --> 25:56.360
His feet are probably about one finger segment longer than mine.

643
25:56.560 --> 25:58.360
As for the width, probably...

644
25:59.150 --> 26:00.750
half a finger segment wider.

645
26:02.280 --> 26:03.280
Get up.

646
26:04.430 --> 26:05.830
Come, put your foot here.

647
26:06.580 --> 26:08.110
One finger segment longer,

648
26:09.040 --> 26:10.640
half a finger segment wider.

649
26:11.430 --> 26:12.190
All right.

650
26:25.150 --> 26:26.320
Now tell me,

651
26:26.670 --> 26:29.230
what else did Chairman Mao say to you?

652
26:29.840 --> 26:30.800
When I arrived,

653
26:31.230 --> 26:32.490
Chairman Mao and Ms. He

654
26:32.800 --> 26:34.840
were already standing there waiting for me.

655
26:34.840 --> 26:36.040
Ms. He was there, too?

656
27:07.120 --> 27:08.040
Enlai,

657
27:08.560 --> 27:10.360
take a break. Let's eat first.

658
27:10.670 --> 27:11.390
All right.

659
27:35.880 --> 27:36.990
Come take a look.

660
27:38.880 --> 27:39.760
What?

661
27:45.950 --> 27:47.320
Where did these come from?

662
27:47.320 --> 27:49.600
These little cakes have quite a story behind them.

663
27:49.600 --> 27:51.460
During the Battle of Zhiluo Town,

664
27:51.560 --> 27:53.090
Chen Geng injured his hand.

665
27:53.520 --> 27:55.190
When Xu Haidong heard about it,

666
27:55.190 --> 27:57.430
he went to great lengths to buy a small bag of sorghum

667
27:57.430 --> 27:59.170
and sent someone to deliver it to Chen Geng

668
27:59.170 --> 28:01.320
as a gift for his former commander.

669
28:01.710 --> 28:04.990
Back when Chen Geng was a division commander in the 4th Front Army,

670
28:04.990 --> 28:07.990
Xu Haidong commanded one of his main regiments.

671
28:09.320 --> 28:11.120
How did that sorghum turn into these cakes

672
28:11.120 --> 28:12.430
and end up here with me?

673
28:13.080 --> 28:14.630
Chen Geng couldn't bear to eat them.

674
28:14.630 --> 28:17.150
He gave most of them to the wounded in the hospital.

675
28:17.150 --> 28:18.610
There were just a few left.

676
28:18.630 --> 28:21.430
He said he wanted to share some with his former commander, too.

677
28:21.430 --> 28:22.990
And that's how these little cakes

678
28:22.990 --> 28:24.650
ended up right in front of you.

679
28:26.360 --> 28:28.230
We can't accept these cakes.

680
28:29.910 --> 28:32.350
You know what Chen Geng is like.

681
28:33.670 --> 28:34.710
But I told him

682
28:34.910 --> 28:36.630
we'd just borrow these cakes.

683
28:38.430 --> 28:39.320
Borrow them?

684
28:40.520 --> 28:41.320
Enlai,

685
28:41.430 --> 28:43.690
you really need some extra nourishment.

686
28:45.320 --> 28:46.630
I have a suggestion.

687
28:46.830 --> 28:48.940
Comrade He Zizhen is pregnant.

688
28:49.230 --> 28:51.320
She needs extra nourishment even more than I do.

689
28:51.320 --> 28:52.920
Why don't we send these cakes

690
28:53.280 --> 28:54.950
to Comrade He Zizhen instead?

691
28:55.080 --> 28:56.080
What do you think?

692
28:57.230 --> 28:57.800
Jin Biao.

693
28:57.950 --> 28:58.560
Yes!

694
28:59.230 --> 28:59.950
Ms. Deng.

695
28:59.990 --> 29:01.040
Vice Chairman Zhou.

696
29:01.040 --> 29:02.380
Please take these sorghum cakes

697
29:02.380 --> 29:03.660
to Comrade Zizhen.

698
29:03.820 --> 29:04.650
Yes, madam.

699
29:05.990 --> 29:06.990
Go on, quickly.

700
29:11.950 --> 29:14.210
Drink the porridge while it's still hot.

701
29:16.880 --> 29:18.480
I'll have to think carefully

702
29:19.320 --> 29:20.760
about what else I can find

703
29:20.800 --> 29:23.060
to help you get some proper nourishment.

704
29:25.760 --> 29:26.670
No need to look.

705
29:27.710 --> 29:29.970
We've already got something right here.

706
29:41.970 --> 29:43.400
I'm not eating it. You eat.

707
29:43.400 --> 29:45.260
You need to regain your strength.

708
29:45.840 --> 29:47.840
I've recovered quite well already.

709
29:47.880 --> 29:49.210
If you don't believe me,

710
29:49.330 --> 29:51.130
I'll show you some kung fu moves.

711
30:02.520 --> 30:03.560
Watch this.

712
31:05.410 --> 31:06.670
See? I wasn't kidding.

713
32:18.430 --> 32:21.080
From December 17, 1935,

714
32:21.120 --> 32:22.270
to the 25th,

715
32:22.800 --> 32:23.670
the CPC Central Committee

716
32:23.670 --> 32:24.630
held an enlarged Politburo meeting

717
32:24.630 --> 32:26.800
in Wayaobu (now Zichang City)

718
32:27.120 --> 32:30.630
to discuss and formulate the Party's strategic line and military strategy.

719
32:30.630 --> 32:31.490
At the meeting,

720
32:31.560 --> 32:33.520
Lin Yuying,

721
32:33.520 --> 32:34.600
the CPC representative to the Comintern,

722
32:34.600 --> 32:36.090
conveyed the resolutions

723
32:36.120 --> 32:38.470
of the Seventh Comintern Congress and explained

724
32:38.470 --> 32:41.190
how the CPC delegation had issued the August 1 Declaration.

725
32:41.190 --> 32:42.950
The participants conducted a comprehensive analysis

726
32:42.950 --> 32:44.710
of the domestic political situation.

727
32:44.710 --> 32:45.800
They unanimously agreed

728
32:45.800 --> 32:47.190
that Japanese imperialism

729
32:47.190 --> 32:49.470
was preparing to annex all of China,

730
32:49.910 --> 32:52.190
turning the entire country from a semi-colony

731
32:52.190 --> 32:55.190
of various imperialist powers into a colony of Japan.

732
32:55.800 --> 32:58.910
This was the defining feature of the current political situation.

733
32:58.910 --> 33:00.190
The Communist Party of China

734
33:00.190 --> 33:02.560
is the vanguard of the Chinese proletariat.

735
33:01.380 --> 33:04.170
[Lin Yuying (Zhang Hao), Member of the CPC Delegation to the Comintern]

736
33:02.760 --> 33:05.320
It is also the vanguard of the entire Chinese nation.

737
33:05.320 --> 33:07.630
We must fight against the sectarian tendency

738
33:07.630 --> 33:10.490
within the Party to shut ourselves off from others.

739
33:10.600 --> 33:11.470
Our task

740
33:11.560 --> 33:12.610
[Deng Fa, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee,

741
33:11.760 --> 33:14.230
is not only to unite all forces

742
33:12.610 --> 33:13.670
[Director of the State Political Security Bureau]

743
33:14.230 --> 33:16.080
that can be mobilized against Japan,

744
33:16.080 --> 33:17.100
but also to win over

745
33:17.100 --> 33:20.150
every possible ally in the fight against Japanese aggression.

746
33:20.150 --> 33:22.950
We must ensure that people across the country contribute whatever they can:

747
33:22.950 --> 33:25.300
manpower, money, weapons,

748
33:25.560 --> 33:27.080
or knowledge.

749
33:27.260 --> 33:29.330
We must leave no patriotic Chinese

750
33:29.350 --> 33:31.870
outside the united front against Japan.

751
33:32.190 --> 33:33.950
This is the Party's general strategy

752
33:33.950 --> 33:37.280
for building the broadest possible national united front.

753
33:37.710 --> 33:40.190
The meeting also laid out the Party's policies on establishing a national defense government

754
33:40.190 --> 33:41.600
and an anti-Japanese united army,

755
33:41.600 --> 33:43.630
transforming the Soviet Republic of Workers and Peasants

756
33:43.630 --> 33:45.990
into a Soviet People's Republic,

757
33:46.360 --> 33:48.950
and expanding and consolidating

758
33:48.990 --> 33:51.800
the Communist Party.

759
33:55.110 --> 33:56.000
Comrades,

760
33:56.450 --> 33:59.730
we will put the above resolutions

761
33:59.750 --> 34:01.520
on the current political situation

762
34:01.520 --> 34:03.600
and the Party's tasks to a vote

763
34:03.800 --> 34:06.630
at the end of this meeting.

764
34:06.630 --> 34:09.030
Now, let's move on to the next agenda item:

765
34:09.679 --> 34:13.070
determining our Party's military strategy

766
34:13.070 --> 34:14.550
under the new circumstances.

767
34:14.550 --> 34:15.199
Next,

768
34:15.199 --> 34:16.580
I'd like to invite Comrade Mao Zedong

769
34:16.429 --> 34:19.030
[Luofu (Zhang Wentian), General Leader of CPC Central Committee]

770
34:16.690 --> 34:19.670
to deliver a report on military strategy.

771
34:25.679 --> 34:28.800
Before outlining our strategic approach,

772
34:29.239 --> 34:30.639
I'd like to discuss

773
34:31.239 --> 34:33.219
the views of one of our comrades.

774
34:34.110 --> 34:35.159
This comrade

775
34:35.360 --> 34:37.840
has looked at the dire situation in northern Shaanxi

776
34:37.840 --> 34:40.639
and concluded that its barren land

777
34:40.800 --> 34:42.650
cannot sustain all of us.

778
34:44.679 --> 34:45.840
And that's not to mention

779
34:45.840 --> 34:47.679
the threat posed by Chiang Kai-shek's

780
34:47.679 --> 34:49.480
100,000 troops surrounding us.

781
34:49.719 --> 34:51.989
So he has reached the following conclusion:

782
34:51.739 --> 34:54.199
[Mao Zedong, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo,]

783
34:52.210 --> 34:54.060
We cannot stay here for long.

784
34:54.199 --> 34:55.429
[Chairman of the Central Executive Committee of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

785
34:55.429 --> 34:56.670
[Chairman of the Northwest Revolutionary Miliary Commission of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

786
34:55.540 --> 34:58.670
He proposes abandoning the Shaanxi-Gansu base

787
34:58.760 --> 35:00.560
and moving to southern Shaanxi,

788
35:00.640 --> 35:04.160
using the Qinling Mountains as our rear base to wage guerrilla warfare.

789
35:04.160 --> 35:06.010
What do you all think?

790
35:07.510 --> 35:09.320
Is there really any need to discuss this?

791
35:09.320 --> 35:10.990
We absolutely cannot abandon

792
35:11.110 --> 35:13.200
the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base.

793
35:13.200 --> 35:14.280
I oppose it, too.

794
35:14.430 --> 35:15.590
We've learned the hard way what it's like to fight

795
35:15.590 --> 35:18.160
without a base area during the Long March.

796
35:18.360 --> 35:19.620
We've finally secured

797
35:19.880 --> 35:21.680
a foothold in northern Shaanxi.

798
35:22.070 --> 35:24.030
How can we just give it up?

799
35:24.430 --> 35:25.640
What we're discussing now

800
35:25.640 --> 35:26.640
is not whether to abandon

801
35:26.640 --> 35:28.550
the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base,

802
35:28.550 --> 35:30.800
but how to consolidate

803
35:30.800 --> 35:32.390
and strengthen it.

804
35:34.070 --> 35:35.680
It seems we're all

805
35:35.320 --> 35:37.490
[Zhou Enlai, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee Politburo,]

806
35:35.840 --> 35:37.470
in agreement on this point.

807
35:37.490 --> 35:39.670
[Vice Chairman of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

808
35:37.580 --> 35:40.820
We all support consolidating the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base.

809
35:40.820 --> 35:41.800
Comrade Zedong,

810
35:42.320 --> 35:44.540
please share your proposed

811
35:44.560 --> 35:46.430
military strategy with everyone.

812
35:46.430 --> 35:47.390
All right.

813
35:48.720 --> 35:51.510
Our main task now

814
35:51.590 --> 35:54.200
is to consolidate the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base.

815
35:54.200 --> 35:55.910
So my military strategy

816
35:56.200 --> 35:58.260
will be built around that objective.

817
35:59.290 --> 36:00.940
[Guo Hongtao, Deputy Secretary of the CPC Shaanxi-Gansu-Shanxi Provincial Committee]

818
36:01.280 --> 36:02.390
My proposal is

819
36:03.390 --> 36:07.760
to direct the Red Army's next major military campaign

820
36:08.510 --> 36:09.680
eastward.

821
36:09.760 --> 36:11.470
We should concentrate our main forces,

822
36:11.470 --> 36:12.720
cross the Yellow River to the east,

823
36:12.720 --> 36:15.760
and launch an expedition into Shanxi.

824
36:15.840 --> 36:18.470
From there, we can move north into Suiyuan

825
36:18.510 --> 36:19.570
or east into Hebei,

826
36:19.590 --> 36:20.840
heading straight for the anti-Japanese front

827
36:20.840 --> 36:22.640
to fight the Japanese directly.

828
36:27.430 --> 36:29.510
[Li Weihan, Minister of the CPC Central Organization Department]

829
36:28.080 --> 36:29.590
We're already in such a difficult position.

830
36:29.590 --> 36:31.030
And now you want to launch an eastern expedition?

831
36:31.030 --> 36:33.550
We can't even be sure we can hold our base.

832
36:33.220 --> 36:35.220
[Wu Liangping, Deputy Minister of the CPC Central Publicity Department]

833
36:33.720 --> 36:35.310
How are we supposed to fight the Japanese?

834
36:35.310 --> 36:36.510
[Liu Shaoqi, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee,]

835
36:35.390 --> 36:36.030
Exactly.

836
36:36.060 --> 36:38.420
Our troops would have to pass through Shanxi first.

837
36:36.510 --> 36:37.720
[Chairman of the Northwest Executive Bureau of the All-China Federation of Trade Unions]

838
36:38.590 --> 36:40.250
Given the state of our forces,

839
36:40.280 --> 36:41.390
can we really afford to fight?

840
36:41.390 --> 36:42.380
The situation certainly is difficult.

841
36:42.380 --> 36:44.910
This issue deserves careful consideration.

842
36:47.430 --> 36:48.430
Comrade Zedong,

843
36:48.990 --> 36:51.590
could you explain your reasoning to everyone?

844
36:54.070 --> 36:57.060
It seems quite a few people are opposed.

845
37:00.070 --> 37:01.400
Perhaps we should first

846
37:01.880 --> 37:03.440
hear everyone's views.

847
37:16.430 --> 37:18.490
I disagree with Comrade Mao Zedong's

848
37:18.550 --> 37:20.900
proposed strategy of launching an eastern expedition.

849
37:20.900 --> 37:21.710
I believe

850
37:21.480 --> 37:24.480
[Bo Gu (Qin Bangxian), Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo]

851
37:21.770 --> 37:25.280
the Red Army's main forces have only just completed the Long March

852
37:25.280 --> 37:26.910
and have yet to recover their strength.

853
37:26.910 --> 37:28.070
Under these circumstances,

854
37:28.070 --> 37:31.160
we should avoid fighting a superior enemy.

855
37:31.390 --> 37:32.310
For now,

856
37:33.110 --> 37:35.200
our first priority should be

857
37:35.240 --> 37:37.910
to consolidate the Shaanxi-Gansu revolutionary base

858
37:37.910 --> 37:40.430
and seek further expansion once it is secure.

859
37:40.430 --> 37:41.550
As for the direction of expansion,

860
37:41.550 --> 37:43.930
I propose moving toward Ningxia and Gansu,

861
37:43.930 --> 37:45.880
where the enemy is relatively weak,

862
37:45.880 --> 37:48.430
and then advancing further into Xinjiang.

863
37:48.990 --> 37:50.320
I want to stress one point.

864
37:50.320 --> 37:51.650
What I said just now was:

865
37:51.760 --> 37:54.010
consolidate first, then expand.

866
37:54.880 --> 37:58.940
I believe expanding westward once our base is secure

867
38:01.110 --> 38:02.370
is the right approach.

868
38:02.800 --> 38:04.840
Once we reach Ningxia,

869
38:04.860 --> 38:06.340
we can head north

870
38:06.800 --> 38:09.360
and establish direct contact with the Soviet Union,

871
38:09.360 --> 38:12.320
which would allow us to obtain Soviet technical assistance.

872
38:11.990 --> 38:14.280
[Wang Jiaxiang, Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee,]

873
38:12.360 --> 38:13.240
Furthermore,

874
38:13.320 --> 38:15.390
this is also the direction

875
38:14.280 --> 38:16.580
[Director of the General Political Department of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission of the Chinese Soviet Republic]

876
38:15.640 --> 38:17.100
Comrade Stalin supports.

877
38:19.110 --> 38:20.570
I'd like to add something.

878
38:20.640 --> 38:22.280
Comrade Peng Dehuai wrote in his telegram

879
38:22.280 --> 38:24.030
that his strategic proposal

880
38:24.200 --> 38:25.880
is to launch a feint eastward,

881
38:26.030 --> 38:27.320
drawing Yan Xishan's troops

882
38:27.320 --> 38:28.550
out of northern Shaanxi

883
38:28.550 --> 38:30.990
so we can eliminate the remaining enemy forces there.

884
38:30.990 --> 38:32.800
After consolidating our base,

885
38:32.990 --> 38:36.990
when the opportunity arises, we can move north toward the Soviet Union.

886
38:37.280 --> 38:38.030
In my earlier

887
38:38.200 --> 38:40.800
correspondence with Comrade Zedong,

888
38:40.880 --> 38:42.720
we discussed this very issue.

889
38:42.910 --> 38:45.030
Comrade Zedong did not oppose

890
38:45.200 --> 38:47.070
the strategy of moving north toward the Soviet Union

891
38:47.070 --> 38:49.390
to seek Soviet technical assistance.

892
38:49.590 --> 38:51.320
I agree with that strategy.

893
38:51.510 --> 38:54.950
What I disagree with is the timing and the route.

894
38:55.110 --> 38:56.680
After our eastern expedition,

895
38:56.680 --> 38:58.160
if circumstances permit,

896
38:58.280 --> 39:01.510
we can move north through Shanxi or Suiyuan

897
39:02.430 --> 39:05.240
and then carry out our original plan of approaching the Soviet Union.

898
39:05.240 --> 39:06.280
But if we do that,

899
39:06.360 --> 39:09.280
our Red Army's main forces will all be fighting in Shanxi.

900
39:09.280 --> 39:11.510
If that leaves our base undefended,

901
39:11.680 --> 39:12.990
who will protect it?

902
39:13.240 --> 39:15.880
If we can't even consolidate our revolutionary base,

903
39:15.880 --> 39:17.810
how can we talk about expanding it?

904
39:17.840 --> 39:18.800
Comrade Zedong,

905
39:19.110 --> 39:20.710
you were the first to propose

906
39:20.840 --> 39:22.510
that we should consolidate our base before expanding,

907
39:22.510 --> 39:23.990
advancing in successive waves.

908
39:23.990 --> 39:26.590
And that strategy has proven effective.

909
39:26.880 --> 39:28.360
Then why did you abandon that very strategy

910
39:28.360 --> 39:30.420
once we arrived in northern Shaanxi?

911
39:30.470 --> 39:32.240
Times have changed. Circumstances are different.

912
39:32.240 --> 39:33.800
We can't cling to old methods.

913
39:33.800 --> 39:35.590
If a strategy has proven effective, we should stick to it.

914
39:35.590 --> 39:36.800
Comrade Zedong.

915
39:36.990 --> 39:37.910
Comrade Bo Gu,

916
39:37.990 --> 39:39.650
I'd like to share my thoughts.

917
39:43.270 --> 39:46.190
I support Comrade Mao Zedong's position.

918
39:43.960 --> 39:45.500
[Kai Feng (He Kequan), Alternate Member of the Politburo of the CPC Central Committee]

919
39:47.240 --> 39:49.760
If we marched north to fight the Japanese

920
39:50.320 --> 39:52.880
and made establishing an Anti-Japanese National United Front

921
39:52.880 --> 39:54.280
our overall strategy,

922
39:54.360 --> 39:57.070
then where else should we go

923
39:57.110 --> 39:59.310
if not toward the anti-Japanese front?

924
39:59.320 --> 40:00.800
As for the Soviet Union,

925
40:00.910 --> 40:03.640
Comrade Stalin merely said he did not oppose

926
40:03.720 --> 40:06.320
our expanding toward areas closer to the Soviet Union.

927
40:06.320 --> 40:08.760
But our specific strategy

928
40:08.910 --> 40:11.590
must be based on the realities on the ground.

929
40:11.840 --> 40:15.510
There's nothing inherently wrong

930
40:15.590 --> 40:18.590
with Comrade Mao Zedong's proposed timing and route.

931
40:18.900 --> 40:22.420
We should consider the balance of forces between the enemy and ourselves.

932
40:20.330 --> 40:21.870
[Li De, Comintern Military Advisor and Instructor at the Red Army University]

933
40:22.590 --> 40:23.840
No matter which direction we choose to advance,

934
40:23.840 --> 40:24.990
it will be dangerous.

935
40:24.990 --> 40:26.250
Comrade Li De believes

936
40:26.390 --> 40:27.280
we should consider

937
40:27.280 --> 40:28.840
the balance of forces between the enemy and ourselves.

938
40:28.840 --> 40:30.390
No matter which direction we choose,

939
40:30.390 --> 40:31.590
it will be dangerous.

940
40:31.880 --> 40:32.950
His position is that

941
40:32.950 --> 40:35.070
given our army's current weakness,

942
40:35.110 --> 40:38.390
we should focus first on expanding our revolutionary base.

943
40:38.390 --> 40:39.280
Comrade Li De,

944
40:39.320 --> 40:41.290
you're advocating a purely defensive strategy again.

945
40:41.290 --> 40:42.200
I'm afraid Chiang Kai-shek

946
40:42.200 --> 40:43.880
won't give us that luxury.

947
40:44.030 --> 40:46.030
But does the Red Army have

948
40:46.910 --> 40:49.990
the strength to expand beyond our current base?

949
40:49.990 --> 40:51.720
But does the Red Army have

950
40:51.720 --> 40:53.680
the strength to expand beyond our current base?

951
40:52.070 --> 40:54.420
[Deng Yingchao, Chief of the CPC Central Committee's Confidential Communications Section]

952
40:53.680 --> 40:55.110
We can barely afford enough food to eat.

953
40:55.110 --> 40:56.570
How much cotton do all of us

954
40:56.640 --> 40:58.920
here have between us, anyway?

955
40:59.460 --> 41:00.990
How much cotton do all of us

956
41:00.990 --> 41:03.290
here have between us, anyway?

957
41:18.510 --> 41:19.370
How about this?

958
41:19.550 --> 41:21.840
Let's adjourn for today.

959
41:22.030 --> 41:24.240
Everyone, go back and get some rest.

960
41:24.560 --> 41:26.320
We'll resume the meeting tomorrow

961
41:26.320 --> 41:28.390
and continue our discussion.

962
41:28.510 --> 41:29.640
Meeting adjourned.

963
41:52.110 --> 41:54.680
When major issues arise within the Party,

964
41:54.880 --> 41:57.360
it's only natural in a democracy

965
41:57.390 --> 42:00.250
for people to hold different views and debate them.

966
42:00.590 --> 42:04.590
Everyone is looking at these issues from the perspective of

967
42:04.640 --> 42:06.360
the success or failure of our cause.

968
42:06.360 --> 42:09.030
Sometimes, having more differing opinions

969
42:09.070 --> 42:10.470
actually helps us

970
42:10.550 --> 42:13.680
see the situation more clearly and comprehensively.

971
42:14.200 --> 42:15.160
Enlai,

972
42:16.990 --> 42:18.550
are you worried

973
42:19.110 --> 42:22.070
that I won't accept opinions that differ from mine?

974
42:23.320 --> 42:26.470
There's a widespread sentiment right now.

975
42:26.800 --> 42:31.160
We've finally completed the Long March

976
42:31.280 --> 42:33.550
and found a foothold here in northern Shaanxi.

977
42:33.550 --> 42:36.070
People simply don't want to move again.

978
42:38.030 --> 42:40.160
But the situation in northern Shaanxi

979
42:40.470 --> 42:42.280
is different from that in Ruijin.

980
42:42.280 --> 42:44.280
If we keep applying the Ruijin model

981
42:44.510 --> 42:46.510
of consolidating our base before expanding,

982
42:46.510 --> 42:47.880
we may end up

983
42:48.280 --> 42:50.430
unable to consolidate it at all,

984
42:51.070 --> 42:52.550
let alone expand.

985
42:52.880 --> 42:54.880
That's why I'm adapting our strategy to local conditions

986
42:54.880 --> 42:56.410
and changing the approach.

987
42:56.840 --> 42:59.110
We must expand to consolidate our base.

988
42:59.550 --> 43:01.110
Launching the Eastern Expedition

989
43:01.110 --> 43:02.950
is a plan I've been considering for a long time.
